title: The Strike Bulletin
subtitle: The papers are silent. Ours need not be.
view-if: crisis_kapp = 1 or crisis_ruhr = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Strike Bulletin

The printers are on strike, and *Die Rote Fahne* is banned anyway. But our comrades have a hand press in a cellar in Wedding, and the strikers are hungry for news.

- @bulletin: Print a daily strike bulletin.
- @expose: Expose the SPD's deals with the generals.
- @letter: Print the Zentrale's own debate, warts and all.

@bulletin
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Keeps the strikers informed and our name in front of them.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.crisis_momentum += 5;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Every morning, a single sheet: where the strike holds, where the troops are, what the committees demand. It is passed from hand to hand until it falls apart.

@expose
subtitle: The Left's line. True enough, but it divides the strikers.
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis_momentum -= 3;
Q.militancy += 3;
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

We print what the SPD ministers said to the generals in Dresden and Stuttgart. The workers read it, and some of them stop trusting the strike committees.

@letter
subtitle: The party will argue in public. Unity suffers; honesty is respected.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity -= 4;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.uspd_relation += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

We print the criticisms from inside the party alongside the Zentrale's line. Readers outside the party are surprised: the communists can admit a mistake.
